From: Miures Manager <contact@miures.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 21:51:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] Data Analytics audit, phase 4: intelligent report builder
 and animated story

The Reports tab gets "Build with Rescript": the researcher states the
objective, key questions, audience, tone and scope; the builder drafts a report
(and optionally a story) ONLY from the saved analyses and their computed
results, shows a review (what was chosen and why, each chart's reason and
denominator, what was left out and why, key questions no analysis answers) and
saves nothing until Create.

- reportBuilder: usability checks, ranking against the key questions, chart per
  question (adviseChart), captions from the analyses' own insights, scenes in
  story order, per-scene regenerate keeping a still-valid chart choice, a model
  interpretation gated sentence by sentence against the results' numbers.
- storyHtml: the story as one self-contained animated HTML file (inline SVG
  charts drawn from the results, transitions, captions, keyboard controls,
  optional narration audio). No video renderer exists, so MP4 is not offered.
- routes: report-builder/draft | scene | story (analytics.edit / .export);
  narration through the existing TTS provider and meter; a story that would
  play blank is refused. Stories are read by publish/snapshot (reportAnalysisIds)
  and shared pages play them from the frozen snapshot in a sandboxed iframe.
- Studio: builder dialog with review, Story tab (preview, edit, chart, hide,
  reorder, regenerate, export), "Play story" on shared links.

Tests: 16 builder + 8 renderer unit tests (26/26 source mutations caught),
parseBrief tests, browser suite scripts/report-builder-test.mjs (22 checks incl.
playback in Chromium and the shared-link story; 8 UI mutations caught).

